warning[W0603]: the mark `Stale` is spelled CapCase
 --> mem:///main.lu:1:28
  |
1 | fn fetch(n: int) -> int ! {Stale, flat(int)} {
  |                            ^^^^^ reads as if there were data to destructure
  |
  = note: payload-free marks are lowercase bare words (`none`, `eof`, `parse`); CapCase is the
    reader's signal that a payload waits inside.

warning[W0603]: the tag `flat` carries a payload but is spelled like a mark
 --> mem:///main.lu:1:35
  |
1 | fn fetch(n: int) -> int ! {Stale, flat(int)} {
  |                                   ^^^^ lowercase reads as nothing-to-destructure
  |
  = note: payload-carrying tags are CapCase and name their payload type (`Parse(ParseErr)`);
    lowercase bare words are reserved for payload-free marks.
